  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c9203b0c5-practice-slot-9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the value of $k$ for which $f(x)=k(x-1)(x-5)$, domain $[1,5]$, is a valid PDF.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=-\\dfrac{3}{32}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\int_1^5 k(x-1)(x-5)\\,dx&=k\\int_1^5(x^2-6x+5)\\,dx\\\\&=k\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}-3x^2+5x\\right]_1^5\\\\&=k\\left(-\\frac{25}{3}-\\frac73\\right)\\\\&=-\\frac{32}{3}k\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{32}{3}k&=1\\\\k&=-\\frac3{32}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck $f(x)\\ge0$: for $1\\le x\\le5$, $(x-1)\\ge0$ and $(x-5)\\le0$, so $(x-1)(x-5)\\le0$. With $k=-\\frac3{32}<0$, $f(x)=-\\frac3{32}(x-1)(x-5)\\ge0$ on $[1,5]$, so $f$ is a valid PDF.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
